                        <provenance type="#rejected"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_330">London,
                            London, Cathedral church of St Paul</orgName> <p>This attribution was
                            rejected in the second edition of Medieval Libraries of Great Britain
                            (1964), although the dagger was inadvertently omitted in the index (see
                            pp. 121, 322). This error was corrected in the Supplement (1987), p.
                            117. The corresponding Medieval Libraries of Great Britain index card,
                            which jointly covers MSS 7, 215, and 218, simply says <q>Reject</q>
                            without further comment. Where MS 7 is concerned, the card probably
                            implicitly served to dispute the claim that M. R. James made in 1932:
                            <q>St Paul's is most probable, though the book is not found in the
                            catalogue.</q></p></provenance>
                    </history>
